  "summary": "14 published single-cell and spatial multiomics papers on tumor immune microenvironments, dated 1-2 Oct 2026; no preprint, code, or industry activity.",
  "synthesis": "Activity is concentrated in published single-cell and spatial multiomics studies of tumor immune microenvironments, all dated 1-2 October 2026. Recurring themes include myeloid and dendritic populations, including RORC-expressing dendritic cells in malignant ascites and single-cell reshaping of glioblastoma tumour-associated macrophages. Lymphoid and NK-CTL programs appear in vaccinated tumor models and in a CTCL scRNA-seq atlas of over 2 million cells from 116 patients. Neutrophil interferon signaling is linked to anti-PD1 resistance in triple-negative breast cancer mouse models. One item reports LNP-formulated synthetic mRNA inducing reversible hematopoietic bias in mice and NHP at supra-clinical doses. The rise ratio of 2.4 rests on 14 published items with no preprint, code, or industry signals. The items do not establish drivers of this rise.",
